cockpit: persist per-mission operator state (dismiss/snooze)

PR A of a two-PR set. Adds a `cockpit_mission_state` table and the routes,
SDK helpers, and UI chips needed for an operator to dismiss or snooze
individual mission cards. PR B will use the same table to track
`planned_sortie_id` when `POST /plan` actually dispatches a sortie
instead of just returning a proposal.

Why
---
The cockpit panel re-derives missions from markdown on every load, so any
operator decision ("not now", "look again tomorrow", "this is launched as
sortie xyz") had nowhere durable to live. Reloading the panel reset the
operator's curation back to the raw markdown view, which is the wrong
default — a roadmap viewer should remember what you've already triaged.

What ships
----------
- New `lib/cockpit-mission-state.ts` — `createCockpitMissionState(db)`
  module exposing `get` / `listForProject` / `set` / `dismiss` / `snooze` /
  `clear`. Keyed on `(project_dir, mission_id)`; upserts use COALESCE so
  setting one field never accidentally clobbers another.
- New SQLite table `cockpit_mission_state` (PK + index, self-initialised
  by the module — mirrors how `sorties` / `feedback` install their own
  schema).
- 3 new routes in `routes/cockpit.ts`:
    - `POST /cockpit/missions/:id/dismiss` (body `{notes?}`)
    - `POST /cockpit/missions/:id/snooze`  (body `{until, notes?}`,
      epoch-ms or ISO 8601; rejects past timestamps)
    - `DELETE /cockpit/missions/:id/state?field={dismissed|snoozed|plannedSortie|all}`
- Existing `GET /cockpit/missions` and `GET /cockpit/missions/:id` now
  merge `state` into each card when the module dep is present. Backward-
  compatible: missions without state get `state: null`.
- SDK helpers: `pd.cockpitDismissMission(...)`, `cockpitSnoozeMission(...)`,
  `cockpitClearMissionState(...)`. `CockpitMissionsResponse.intake` types
  updated.
- Fleet UI panel chips: each mission row gets `Dismiss` and `24h snooze`
  buttons; dismissed/snoozed missions hide from the default view but a
  `Show hidden N` filter brings them back. Dismissed rows render at 55%
  opacity with a chip badge; restore button reverses everything.
- `features.manifest.json` updated for parity.

Validation
----------
- `npx tsc --noEmit` clean.
- 508/508 unit tests pass across cockpit + parity suites (added 9 new
  state-module tests + 7 new route tests).
- `npm run build` in fleet-config-ui clean (935 kB → bundle includes the
  new chip UI + 3 SDK helpers).

Not in this PR
--------------
- `/plan` still returns a proposal only; PR B wires it to actually call
  `spawner.spawn()` + claim mission files + write `planned_sortie_id`
  back to the table this PR introduces.
- Live SSE push for state mutations. The infrastructure exists
  (`/fleet/events`, `/activity/subscribe`) — wiring is a small slice on
  top of this; will be PR C.


